    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "膈關(关,関)" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0008231 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The medial cutaneous branches of the posterior rami of the sixth and seventh thoracic nerves; deeper, their lateral branches." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "dysphagia, hiccup, vomiting, belching, pain and stiffness of the back." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "In the upper back region, at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous process of the seventh thoracic vertebra (T7), 3 B-cun lateral to the posterior median line. Note: BL 46, BL17 and GV9 are located at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous process of the seventh thoracic vertebra (T7)." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture obliquely 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Geguan" ;
    tara-ap:hasSpecificReferenceLocation UBERON:0004632,
