<http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_2645290> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "PC 4" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "[Acupoint Location, Pinyin Label, Chinese Label] WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization (WHO), WHO Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 153. https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/353407",
        "[Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, Indications] Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridians. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7." ;
    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "郄門(门)" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0002386 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The medial antebrachial cutaneous nerve; deeper, the median nerve; deepest, the anterior interosseous nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "cardiac pain, palpitation, epistaxis, hematemesis, hemoptysis, chest pain, furuncle, epilepsy." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the anterior aspect of the forearm, between the tendons of the palmaris longus and the flexor carpi radialis, 5 B-cun proximal to the palmar wrist crease. Note 1: With the fist clenched, the wrist supinated, and the elbow slightly flexed, the two tendons become more prominent. PC4 is located 1 B-cun distal to the midpoint of the line connecting PC3 with PC7. Note 2: If the palmaris longus tendon is not present, PC4 is medial to the flexor carpi radialis tendon." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Ximen" ;
    tara-ap:hasSpecialPointRole <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4598552> ;
    tara-ap:hasSpecificReferenceLocation UBERON:0016496,
        ILX:0795334,
        ILX:0795500 ;
    tara-ap:hasSynonym "HC 4",
        "P 4",
        "PE 4",
        "Per 4",
        "Pericardium 4" ;
    tara-ap:hasVasculatureInformation "The median artery and vein; deeper, the anterior interosseous artery and vein." ;
    tara-ap:isLocatedOnMeridian <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4694897> ;
