    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0001456 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The great auricular nerve and facial nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "deafness, tinnitus, toothache, motor impairment of the temporomandibular joint, mumps, deviation of the eye and mouth." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the face, in the depression between the intertragic notch and the condylar process of the mandible. Note: When the mouth is opened, GB2 is located in the depression anterior to the intertragic notch." ;
