<http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_3226024> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "SI 14" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "[Acupoint Location, Pinyin Label, Chinese Label] WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization (WHO), WHO Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 94. https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/353407",
        "[Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, Indications] Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridians. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7." ;
    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "肩外兪(俞)" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0008231 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "Superficially, the medial cutaneous branches of the posterior rami of the first and second thoracic nerves, the accessory nerve; deeper, the dorsal scapular nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "aching of the shoulder and back, pain and rigidity of the neck." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "In the upper back region, at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous process of the first thoracic vertebra (T1), 3 B-cun lateral to the posterior median line. Note 1: SI14 is located at the intersection of two imaginary lines: the vertical line of the medial extremity of the spine of the scapula and the horizontal line inferior to the spinous process of the first thoracic vertebra (T1). Note 2: SI14 is located at the same level as BL11, gV13, and the inferior border of the spinous process of the first thoracic vertebra (T1)." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture obliquely 0.3-0.7 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Jianwaishu" ;
