    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "養(养)老" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0002386 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The anastomotic branches of the posterior antebrachial cutaneous nerve and the dorsal branch of the ulnar nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "blurred vision, pain in the shoulder, elbow and arm." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the posteromedial aspect of the forearm, in the depression radial to the head of the ulnar bone, 1 B-cun proximal to the dorsal wrist crease. Note: With the palm facing downwards, press the highest point of the head of ulnar bone with a finger, and then turn the palm towards the chest; SI6 is located at the cleft between the bones where the finger slides." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Yanglao" ;
