<http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_4369524> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "ST 11" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "[Acupoint Location, Pinyin Label, Chinese Label] WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization (WHO), WHO Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 51. https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/353407",
        "[Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, Indications] Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridians. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7." ;
    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "氣(气,気)舍(舎)" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0000974 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The medial supraclavicular nerve and the muscular branch of ansa cervicalis." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "sore throat, pain and rigidity of the neck, asthma, hiccup, goiter." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "In the anterior region of the neck, in the lesser supraclavicular fossa, superior to the sternal end of the clavicle, in the depression between the sternal and clavicular heads of the sternocleidomastoid muscle. Note 1: The sternocleidomastoid muscle is more distinct when the head is turned to the opposite side against resistance. Note 2: ST11 is located superior to the clavicle, inferior to St9." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Qishe" ;
    tara-ap:hasRelatedArtery UBERON:0010197 ;
    tara-ap:hasRelatedNerve ILX:0797523,
        ILX:0797524 ;
    tara-ap:hasRelatedVein UBERON:0001104 ;
    tara-ap:hasSpecificReferenceLocation UBERON:0001105,
        UBERON:0001128,
        ILX:0795293 ;
    tara-ap:hasSynonym "S 11",
        "Stomach 11" ;
    tara-ap:hasVasculatureInformation "Superficially, the anterior jugular vein; deeper, the common carotid artery." ;
    tara-ap:isLocatedOnMeridian <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_6221269> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
