    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "low back pain, spasm of the gastrocnemius, hemorrhoids, constipation, beriberi." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the posterior aspect of the leg, at the connecting point of the calcaneal tendon with the two muscle bellies of the gastrocnemius muscle. Note: With the leg stretched (plantar flexion) or the heel up, BL57 is located at the sharp angled depression inferior to the muscle belly of the gastrocnemius muscle. the two heads of the gastrocnemius muscle are separated to make a lambda shape (Λ)." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.8-1.2 inches. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Chengshan" ;
    tara-ap:hasSpecificReferenceLocation UBERON:0001388,
        UBERON:0003701 ;
    tara-ap:hasSynonym "B 57",
        "Bladder 57",
        "UB 57",
        "Urinary Bladder 57" ;
    tara-ap:hasVasculatureInformation "The small saphenous vein; deeper, the posterior tibial artery and vein." ;
    tara-ap:isLocatedOnMeridian <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_7525476> ;
