<http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_5797983> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "BL 15" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "[Acupoint Location, Pinyin Label, Chinese Label] WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization (WHO), WHO Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 107. https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/353407",
        "[Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, Indications] Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridians. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7." ;
    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "心兪(俞)" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0008231 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The medial cutaneous branches of the posterior rami of the fifth and sixth thoracic nerves; deeper, their lateral branches." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "cardiac pain, panic, loss of memory, palpitation, cough, spitting of blood, nocturnal emission, night sweat, mania, epilepsy." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "In the upper back region, at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous pro- cess of the fifth thoracic vertebra (T5), 1.5 B-cun lateral to the posterior median line." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture obliquely 0.5-0.7 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Xinshu" ;
