    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "小海(海)" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0001461 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The branches of the medial antebrachial cutaneous nerve, the ulnar nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "headache, swelling of the cheek, pain in the nape, shoulder, arm and elbow, epilepsy." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the posteromedial aspect of the elbow, in the depression between the olecranon and the medial epicondyle of the humerus bone. Note: When the elbow is slightly flexed, SI 8 is located in the groove for the ulnar nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
