    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The branches of the superficial peroneal nerve and the deep peroneal nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "lower abdominal pain, backache referring to the testis, mastitis, numbness and paralysis of the lower extremities." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the anterior aspect of the leg, on the line connecting ST35 with ST41, 9 B-cun inferior to ST35. Note: ST39 is located on the tibialis anterior muscle, at the same level as GB35 and gB36." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
