    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation ILX:0795303 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "The branch of the iliohypogastric nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "retention and dribbling of urine, enuresis, nocturnal emission, impotence, morbid leukorrhea, irregular menstruation, dysmenorrhea, hernia." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the lower abdomen, superior to the pubic symphysis, on the anterior median line." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Great care should be taken to puncture the points from Qugu (CV 2) to Shangwan (CV 13) of this meridian in pregnant women. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
