    tara-ap:hasChineseLabel "大陵" ;
    tara-ap:hasGeneralSurfaceLocation UBERON:0004452 ;
    tara-ap:hasInnervationInformation "Deeper, the median nerve." ;
    tara-ap:hasListedIndications "cardiac pain, palpitation, stomachache, vomiting, mental disorder, epilepsy, stuffy chest, pain in the hypochondriac region, convulsion, insomnia, irritability, foul breath." ;
    tara-ap:hasLocationalDescription "On the anterior aspect of the wrist, between the tendons of palmaris longus and the flexor carpi radialis, on the palmar wrist crease. Note: With the fist clenched, the wrist slightly flexed, the two tendons become more prominent. PC7 is located at the midpoint of the palmar wrist crease, between the tendons of palmaris longus and the flexor carpi radialis, at the same level as Ht7, at the proximal extremity of the pisiform bone." ;
    tara-ap:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara-ap:hasPinyinLabel "Daling" ;
    tara-ap:hasSpecialPointRole <http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/TARA_1840369>,
